{"url": "https://www.rowan.edu/admissions/how-to-apply/international-students/international-policies/index.html", "final_url": "https://www.rowan.edu/admissions/how-to-apply/international-students/international-policies/", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "About\nAbout\nFast Facts\nLeadership\nOur Location\nOur Campuses\nCareers\nFeatured Links\nRowan Voices\nPlan a Visit\nAcademics\nAcademics\nDegrees & Programs\nColleges & Schools\nStudent Success\nBooks & Gear\nCourses, Schedules, & Registration\nStudy Abroad\nRowan Online\nFeatured Links\nAcademic Calendar\nRowan Library\nAdmissions & Aid\nAdmissions & Aid\nHow To Apply\nFirst-Year Admissions\nTransfer Admissions\nGraduate Admissions\nMilitary & Veteran Admissions\nTuition & Aid\nOpen Houses & Campus Visits\nFeatured Links\nAlternate Admissions Paths\nApplication Calendar & Fees\nStudent Life\nStudent Life\nVisit Rowan\nHousing & Dining\nStudent Invlovement\nStudent Organizations\nInternational Center\nAthletics & Sports Recreation\nEntertainment, Art & Culture\nFeatured Links\nCenter for Well-Being\nHealth & Safety\nHealth & Medicine\nHealth & Medicine\nCooper Medical School of Rowan University\nVirtua Health College of Medicine & Life Sciences\nRowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine (DO & PA)\nRita & Larry Salva School of Nursing & Health Professions\nRowan-Virtua School of Translational Biomedical Engineering & Sciences\nShreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (DVM)\nResearch\nResearch\nDivision of University Research\nSouth Jersey Technology Park\nFeatured Links\nResearch Centers & Institutes\nResearch News\nAthletics\nAthletics\nRowan Athletics (NCAA)\nCampus Recreation\nAthletics Facilities\nRequest Info\nVisit\nGive\nApply\nRowan Online\nEXPLORE\nHome\n/\nAdmissions & Aid\n/\nHow to Apply to Rowan\n/\nInternational Students\n/\nInternational Policies\nInternational Policies\nInternational Students\nEnglish Language Requirements\nForeign Credential Evaluations\nInternational Graduate Students\nInternational Policies\nInternational Transfer Admissions\nInternational Undergraduate Students\nScholarships\nRowan considers international applicants students who entered or plan to enter the United States on a non-immigrant visa (e.g., F-1 or J-1) and maintain non-immigrant status throughout their study at Rowan University. This includes those who have submitted residency application documents to USCIS, but have not received formal approval verifying that you have become a permanent resident of the United States.\nDomestic (or U.S.) applicants are students who are United States citizens, approved permanent residents of the United States (\u201cGreen Card\u201d holder), asylees, refugees, undocumented students, or DACA students.\nApplication Fee\nInternational undergraduate applicants (freshmen and transfer applicants): $45.00 (USD) non-refundable\nInternational graduate applicants (masters coursework-only applicants): $65.00 (USD) non-refundable\nEnrollment Deposit\nInternational undergraduate applicants (freshmen and transfer applicants): $100.00 (USD) non-refundable\nInternational graduate applicants (masters coursework-only applicants): $250.00 (USD) non-refundable\nDeposits are required prior to receiving an I-20. Enrollment deposits are applied to students' tuition and fees once enrolled.\nApplication Fee Waiver\nLooking for a waiver? If you already have a foreign credential evaluation from a provider who is a member of NACES, and you submit an official copy during the application process, we will waive the application fee and offer you the opportunity to apply to Rowan free of charge.\nContact\nOffice of International Admissions\nRowan University\nEnterprise Center, 3rd Floor | 225 Rowan Blvd.\nGlassboro, New Jersey, 08028, USA\n(856) 256-5585\ninternational@rowan.edu\nBack To Top\nP: 856-256-4000\n201 Mullica Hill Road\nGlassboro, NJ 08028\nContact Us\nMaps & Directions\nOur Campuses\nQuick Links\nCareers\nLibrary\neCampus Book